WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.972
Use two kinds of safeguards for loops.

00:00:02.972 --> 00:00:09.712
First, define an application-level limit such as max steps equals three.

00:00:09.712 --> 00:00:13.297
This is part of your business or workflow policy.

00:00:13.297 --> 00:00:17.687
For example, allow at most two query rewrites.

00:00:17.687 --> 00:00:22.723
Second, use Lang Graph's recursion limit as a runtime safety net.

00:00:23.324 --> 00:00:25.206
These are not the same thing.

00:00:25.206 --> 00:00:30.036
Max steps expresses what your application considers reasonable.

00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:36.921
The recursion limit protects you if routing logic accidentally creates a cycle you did not expect.

00:00:36.921 --> 00:00:43.656
A healthy workflow should normally stop because its own success or failure conditions are reached.

00:00:43.656 --> 00:00:49.579
The recursion limit should be the emergency brake, not the main way the agent stops.

00:00:50.096 --> 00:00:59.793
Useful stop reasons include evidence sufficient, answer validated, no approved evidence, user clarification required,

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.809
or maximum budget reached.
